== run 1: setup-ide
exit: 1
-- stdout
❌ Error: IDE parameter required

Usage: <GUIDE>/scripts/setup-ide <ide> [--dry-run] [--write-lint] [--root <dir>]

  --dry-run     List the files that would be added, changed or removed; write nothing
  --write-lint  Write required lint configs that are missing (default: report only)
  --root <dir>  Install into <dir> (e.g. a git worktree) using this script's guide
  --capabilities  Print supported features as one line and exit

Supported targets:
  cursor    - Always-on rules → AGENTS.md; scoped rules → .cursor/rules/ (paths→globs)
  claude    - Embed alwaysApply rules in CLAUDE.md, copy others to .claude/rules/
  copilot   - Compile rules/skills to .github/ for VS Code Copilot (also writes AGENTS.md)
  agents    - Write AGENTS.md, plus skills to .agents/skills/ if present
              aliases: openai, codex

Examples:
  <GUIDE>/scripts/setup-ide cursor
  <GUIDE>/scripts/setup-ide claude
  <GUIDE>/scripts/setup-ide copilot
  <GUIDE>/scripts/setup-ide agents

This script copies AI project rules from project-guides/ to your IDE's
configuration directory and validates frontmatter requirements.
